<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Dagger</h1>
<p>Average Length: Approx. 6 inches to 1 foot.
Type of Weapon: Very Close Hand-to-hand.
Commonly used by: All classes.
</p><p>These weapons were not widespread in the army, but most of the people in the Middle Ages had one or more. These weapons were small, usually less than a foot long, but generally very sharp. All different designs were used, and they could be either for throwing or hand-to-hand. They were especially popular among merchants and thieves.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla the dagger is a weapon skill of its own, one of the swords (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>): one-handed, it stabs (a piercing weapon), it leans on dexterity, with some strength, and it is quick, as light weapons are. Nearly every guild teaches it: the assassins, druids and fighters from guild level 0, the conjurers, dark knights, necromancers, paladins, sorcerers and thieves from guild level 0 (up to 80%), the barbarians from guild level 2 and the rangers from guild level 3 (up to 80%). Only the healers don't teach it. Outside the guilds it is also taught by Tue Ironside, in the back room of the inn in Udgaard (anyone, up to 35%), and Kern, a craggy troll who hides in his cave in Galgachus (members of the Thieves' guild only).
</p><p><br />
